As usually, per my self-imposed rule, I've turned into the final form at 
the castle.  However, I didn't genocide @s to keep the genoless conduct 
this time.  The preparation phase was pretty typical, except for a 
stone-to-flesh+esc+"magical energy is released"+luckstone accident.  Uh 
oh.  I've wasted all wands of polymorph I could find, but without the 
spell, I didn't manage to get the stone back through polypiling.  There 
went the wish -- a luckstone with half phys and half spell damage.
(wishing for the EotO was mandatory anyway because it's the only way to 
read the Book).

The only edible relevant ring was regeneration (wooden), so no protection, 
increase damage and the like for me...  Of course, without regeneration, 
the ascension would be impossible (as you regain only 1hp/20 turns when 
polyed).

So ok, I wished for an archon, gave him my +7 Frosty, BDSM, AoLS, etc 
while my former angelic pets got the +7 Firey and +7 Sunsword, quaffed all 
the !s of FH, and there we go...


It turned out that I forgot to take into account the insanely low carrying 
capacity of green slimes.  If you try to carry anything more than two 
potions or five wands, you get stressed -- so, I didn't really bother with 
any equipment.  Without AC and MC, potions can't survive the first fire/ 
cold attack anyway.

The pets: somehow, archons never live long.  They get into unnecessary 
fights all the time, and get burrped in just a few turns after taming.  
Blargh.  On the other hand, both of my original angels survived all the 
way until the very end.  They don't attack any of the really tough 
monsters, but why would I bother if I could slime anyone?
The sliming attack works on 1/4 of all hits, and the only monsters that 
are exempt are green slimes (duh), shades and flaming stuff.  Everything 
else, including ghosts (bug), the Riders, Rodney, demon princes and 
cockatrices goes under just the same...  But then, with green slime's 
shitty physical damage, I needed around ten hits to get rid of any of the 
slimed enemies -- or a single blow from my angels.  We went along nicely, 
I slimed everything in sight while they eradicated the resulting slimes, 
staying away from big nasty stuff that could kill them.  As a result, 
Juiblex was the only big & on my trophies list (even a slime can do that 
1hp of physical damage).

About the nasties, liches turned out to be especially harmless.  They kept 
going into melee all the time instead of staying away, and if you don't 
have anything, what bad can they do?  Archons and ki-rins can at least 
inflict some significant physical damage, but they're not genocidable 
anyway.  In other words, genocides wouldn't be really helpful anyway.

However, the speed was an extreme issue.  Even with the infinite 
haste-self trick[1], a green slime acts about once per two game turns.  It 
makes you pretty vulnerable -- a single mastodon once took 400hp _with 
half damage_.  It even creates a food problem, as food consumption is not 
affected by your speed.  I had a consumption rate of 32/20 (as 
mysteriously my =oPC survived all the way until early Astral), and to 
remain sated, I had to eat all the time.  Somehow, Famine didn't take an 
advantage of this.

Bottom line:
Yes, green slime ascension is possible.  No, black pudding ascension is 
_not_ likely, perhaps except for Marvin with a patched RNG.

